f{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/87/878c78eb8d30fba7850c06358383eb836debee6153612d457e1224ffa1dc6f17.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/a9/a98e35567b90f83d21889c39011386e11a10005f8acacc7e6173cabd83a11128.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares left and $3$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares right and $1$ square down. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares right and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $2$ squares down. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=1$."] [:db/add "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed" :question/answer-fields "0e6263a8-adae-50d6-a19c-aa5847f91b6d"] [:db/add "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed" :question/answer-fields "fdeefe74-c969-5e67-a972-2f614581f19b"] [:db/ensure "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "d651eab0-37dc-5b75-abf4-c4468b0effed"] [:db/add "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969" :answer/id #uuid "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969"] [:db/add "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969" :answer/value "3"] [:db/ensure "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/id #uuid "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79"] [:db/add "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/choices "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969"] [:db/add "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/correct "94f930ea-bd58-5fc7-9879-fe42eff10969"] [:db/ensure "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed" :answer/id #uuid "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed"] [:db/add "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed" :answer/validate] [:db/add "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5"] [:db/add "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/choices "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed"] [:db/add "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/correct "4fab57f8-8f1d-5534-82ed-9551848475ed"] [:db/ensure "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/id #uuid "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c"] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/60/60255b61fdbc0e85d64d02c1ef173c7db1706ffc892b2fca2dfb8a2a62f9416d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/61/6194a056c4fe39746ab072e5ef1de9a581d266918de114beadf0c9cfd6180212.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $1$ square left and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square right and $2$ squares up. Thus $OX=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $3$ squares right and $3$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square right and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=3\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=3$ and $\\mu=-1$."] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/answer-fields "d60bc297-b80e-5105-b886-3bfa677d3f79"] [:db/add "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/answer-fields "0c33878a-99ce-5bad-bdc7-a3f2540f53d5"] [:db/ensure "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "7170985b-076a-5e56-83d9-0fafab8d449c"] [:db/add "0d807693-8ddd-5f63-beea-8b2292ea25e9" :answer/id #uuid "0d807693-8ddd-5f63-beea-8b2292ea25e9"] [:db/add "0d807693-8ddd-5f63-beea-8b2292ea25e9" :answer/type 