9c2347d2ba48f29064b37a9b37bb053e843d991086ff817d3d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/10/1094a82e20624415069d1c56cc6cc13eb1c7269326662b86aae76e7ebc37e832.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $6$ squares left and $3$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares right and $1$ square up. Thus $OX=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square right and $1$ square up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square right and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=1$."] [:db/add "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7" :question/answer-fields "b90d1ebf-c507-5f4e-9f81-f9aca00f6687"] [:db/add "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7" :question/answer-fields "fa052558-217c-5ded-bb12-27cef4b1f430"] [:db/ensure "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "2e2cf952-f121-53ef-8bdf-2a068d3160c7"] [:db/add "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e" :answer/id #uuid "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e"] [:db/add "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e" :answer/value "1"] [:db/ensure "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d"] [:db/add "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/choices "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e"] [:db/add "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/correct "678af90a-d723-58c8-81b1-a65d6bf49d2e"] [:db/ensure "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998" :answer/id #uuid "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998"] [:db/add "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998" :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}"] [:db/ensure "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94"] [:db/add "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/choices "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998"] [:db/add "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/correct "59828ea4-cb8b-573e-a5ac-0d3528737998"] [:db/ensure "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/id #uuid "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8"] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/d8/d8d5a545d88a83236994219393eb998b67abfa5b05e6f7d0f9c26529f168f2b2.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}"] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/70/7052d3c533e32a07ba1e612d92b7b81b74e6aaf34a12f6ca53a7ce0f313ef787.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $1$ square left and $1$ square down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square down. Thus $OX=1|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $6$ squares right and $3$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $4$ squares left and $2$ squares down. Thus $XC=\\frac{3}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=\\mathbf{a}-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=1$ and $\\mu=-\\frac{3}{2}$."] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/answer-fields "ad19ac3f-774d-5722-89f8-16ce4726a10d"] [:db/add "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/answer-fields "f1579a83-b315-593b-aae6-cdb53c753a94"] [:db/ensure "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/questions "66ea80ee-e83a-580d-84c5-654898396cd8"] [:db/ensure 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/validate]]
